<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="card prose">
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="muted">Version <%= noticeVersion %></p>

  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>
    <%= siteName %> is a private photo site run by the child's parents (the
    "guardians") to share photos with invited family. The guardians decide
    what is shared and with whom. There are no ads, no third-party analytics
    or trackers, and nothing is ever sold or shared with anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>The child</h2>
  <p>
    The child in these photos cannot consent for themselves, so we treat
    their privacy as the top priority. Every photo starts out visible only to
    the guardians. Location, camera, and device details are removed from every
    photo when it is uploaded. When the child is older, the guardians can hand
    over or permanently erase the whole archive.
  </p>

  <h2>What we keep about family members</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your account:</strong> email, name, an optional username, and a scrambled (hashed) password.</li>
    <li><strong>What you add:</strong> comments, reactions, personal albums, and photos you send in.</li>
    <li><strong>Downloads:</strong> which photo you downloaded, when, and the first part of your network address. These records are deleted after <%= downloadRetentionDays %> days.</li>
    <li><strong>Security records:</strong> sign-ins and important changes, so the guardians can see if something goes wrong. Details are removed after <%= auditRetentionDays %> days.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage counts:</strong> daily totals, such as how many sign-ins there were and how often each part of the site was used, so the guardians can decide whether the site is worth keeping. These totals do not say who did what, and small counts are hidden. They are deleted after about 13 months.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Downloads are traced</h2>
  <p>
    If the guardians let you download a photo, the copy you get carries a
    hidden reference code and usually a small visible mark. The code does not
    contain your name; only the guardians can look it up. This exists so a
    photo that ends up somewhere it should not be can be traced. Please keep
    downloaded photos private.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Download everything we hold about you: Settings, Export my data.</li>
    <li>Delete your account: Settings, Delete account. You choose whether your comments are removed or kept without your name.</li>
    <li>Photos you already downloaded stay on your device; please delete them if asked.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where data lives</h2>
  <p>
    Photos are encrypted and stored in a private storage bucket. Account data
    is stored in an encrypted database. Both are hosted by our cloud provider
    under a data processing agreement. Backups expire within 30 days, so
    anything deleted is fully gone from backups within that time.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Ask the guardians directly. They can see the security records and act on any request.</p>

  <% if (needsAccept) { %>
    <form method="post" action="/privacy/accept" class="stacked-form">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>" />
      <button type="submit" class="primary-button">I have read this notice</button>
    </form>
  <% } %>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
